WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:08.910
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, a whole bunch
of you requested a video about all my favorite

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:09.910
shows this year.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:17.420
There is a lot of stuff I watch that I don’t
do videos for but for the most part I do videos

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:18.420
for stuff I like the most.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.420
So there aren’t a lot of things I’m in
love with that you won’t see on my channel

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.660
in some shape or form.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.660
So here’s what I’m going to do.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.340
I’ll name my top 10 shows, and for each
of them, I’ll say my favorite episode of

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.340
the year.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:31.730
I’ll have a couple of announcements about
next week’s videos at the end of this.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:36.960
So let’s do the thing!

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.820
Number 10 - Gotham

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:45.469
Amongst the pantheon of new comic book shows
Gotham above all had the highest chance of

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:46.469
sucking.

00:00:46.469 --> 00:00:50.730
It didn’t have Batman or any costumes for
that matter.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:58.460
And one of it’s central characters was a
little kid.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:03.120
What made me start to enjoy it was how much
it embraced the campy aspects of the Batman

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.120
Universe.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.800
And when I say it’s campy, I mean it goes
to that self-aware silly place that the Animated

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.050
Series and the Tim Burton films go to.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.200
Visually there’s a lot of Chris Nolan in
there too.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:17.049
But my eyes are always drawn to the Tim Burton
type scenes when it gets a little crazier.

00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:21.100
Like this scene with Edward Nygma and this
file clerk that he’d like to solve some

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.550
bedroom riddles with.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:24.010
Forget the sexual comedy.

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:27.070
Just look at how they frame this shot and
the set design.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:30.470
Moments like this are really what I like best
about Gotham.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.100
If you wanted to explain Gotham to your friend.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.979
Don’t say it’s Batman without Batman.

00:01:33.979 --> 00:01:36.630
That’s probably the worst way to get someone
excited about it.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:37.990
Tell them it’s Gotham Central.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:42.149
It’s a police procedural set around Detective
Gordon and the Gotham City PD.

00:01:42.149 --> 00:01:47.070
I know, the big question is why didn’t they
just call it Gotham Central.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:50.159
The comic book was super popular and had great
stories.

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:52.630
Answer, probably because of rights issues.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:56.289
I do think a stricter adaptation of Gotham
Central would have been a better show, but

00:01:56.289 --> 00:02:01.040
the stories and the characters in the comics
go beyond what Fox is allowed to do legally.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.299
My Favorite Gotham Episode so far is Episode
9 Harvey Dent.

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:09.080
I feel like you could show that episode to
your friends who are fans of Batman and they’d

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.909
enjoy it because of Harvey Dent.

00:02:10.909 --> 00:02:13.730
And Nicholas D’Agosto did a great job with
the character.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:18.670
Number 9 - South Park

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:23.569
Ever since the series went from 14 episodes
a season down to 10 I feel like the quality

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:24.569
has gone up.

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:25.569
Because the 6 day production schedule they
have is so above and beyond what normal shows

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:26.569
do, Matt and Trey and the rest of the crew
are almost dead by the end of each run.

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:28.730
Live Action shows take an entire week to shoot
an episode and then another two months of

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.680
editing, scoring and post production.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:33.819
Animated shows can take up to 6 months to
finish.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:38.450
South Park writes, animates and finishes each
episode in 6 days.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:42.569
My favorite episode of 2014 is Cock Magic,
although this year there were like 4 episodes

00:02:42.569 --> 00:02:46.629
which I thought were better than almost everything
else on tv ever.

00:02:46.629 --> 00:02:53.659
But that’s because they were topical, informed
and fucking hilarious.

00:02:53.659 --> 00:02:57.530
You don’t need to sell your friends on South
Park, it’s so good it sells itself.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.490
And they make it available to watch everywhere
free.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.420
Number 8 - Agents Of SHIELD

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:03.740
Team Coulson really upped their game.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:05.879
I was already on board during season 1.

00:03:05.879 --> 00:03:10.850
I will freely admit that no matter how ridiculous
or flat this might get, I will still watch

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:16.170
it just because it provides extra context
for the larger workings of the Movies.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:22.190
But they just debuted brand new IP for the
first time on screen.

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:30.590
And that has me excited for what they can
do with other IP in the future.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:37.510
The thing that keeps me connected to the show
on an emotional level is Coulson and his relationships

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:38.510
with the other characters.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.840
He is the anchor of this show, with good cause.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:50.390
I think he’s the most experienced actor
so he does a better job of selling the material,

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:53.650
especially the weirder marvel verse comic
booky stuff.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:57.250
And in real life he’s like a spirit guide
for all the younger actors who are pushing

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.370
themselves to evolve.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:03:59.970
Chloe Bennet as Skye for example.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.850
I love what she’s doing this season but
I want more of it.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.740
I think the show does better when it focuses
on a couple things rather than trying to service

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:05.740
10 different characters at once.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:09.000
The thing to get pumped about is next year,
the back half of this season is going to focus

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.569
more on her and the Inhumans.

00:04:13.569 --> 00:04:19.299
The movie isn’t coming till after Avengers
3, so now is the time to board the ship.

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:23.610
My favorite SHIELD episode this year is Episode
8 Things We Bury.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:28.509
It gives us this amazing montage with our
big villain Whitehall and it’s super personal.

00:04:28.509 --> 00:04:32.860
You have the Ward brothers going all Cain
and Abel, Whitehall destroying Skye’s Mother

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:42.700
and a great performance from Hayley Atwell
as Peggy Carter.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.509
Number 7 - Walking Dead

00:04:44.509 --> 00:04:48.600
The energy from this show mixes so well with
the more pleasant emotions I get from the

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.060
other stuff I watch.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.410
Arrow for instance always makes me feel happy
and excited.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:55.960
But you can’t live on sugar alone.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:59.350
So Walking Dead is the perfect way to balance
myself.

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:01.440
I always feel excited coming away from episodes.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.699
But usually it’s that type of excitement
you feel after you get in a car crash.

00:05:04.699 --> 00:05:07.639
Like you’re having an anxiety attack.

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:10.740
Favorite Episode of this year is the Season
5 Premiere.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.060
Carol wins everything.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:13.979
drop the mic.

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:15.729
Number 6 - Doctor Who

00:05:15.729 --> 00:05:18.680
Far and away my most beloved Science Fiction
series.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:22.190
I did notice a lot of fallout in the online
fandom between the 50th Anniversary Special

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:25.540
last year and the regular series 8 episodes.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:29.940
Doctor Who always has this really strong core
fandom that both loves and hates everything

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:33.890
steven moffat does and will tell you exactly
what they think in all CAPS youtube comments.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.319
But for the 50th last year it was like the
whole world zeroed in on The Special.

00:05:37.319 --> 00:05:39.260
There’s this big disconnect between what’s
popular in the world and what’s popular

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:40.260
online.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:41.260
So Doctor Who might not be as big Internationally
as Game of Thrones or Walking Dead, but the

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.260
online audience is almost as big because people
are so passionate about it.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:44.110
Series 8 was very polarizing and that’s
part of the reason I loved it so much.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.370
Doctor Who isn’t afraid to be ridiculous.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:50.870
It vacillates between really dark serious
stories like Listen and really silly moments

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:54.390
like Cousin It TARDIS.

00:05:54.390 --> 00:06:01.580
I’m much more excited by new ideas than
really amazing action or huge twists in the

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:02.580
plot.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:06.170
So female master and Capaldi’s Doctor made
for a great series.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:09.310
There are so many other things I could say
about Doctor Who this year but I’ll save

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:12.449
some of it for the bonus videos I’m doing
this week.

00:06:12.449 --> 00:06:17.730
The Christmas Special is on December 25th,
for those that don’t know.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:20.940
I’ll try to get at least a few Doctor Who
videos up before that.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.850
So be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:28.520
My favorite Episode this year not including
the Christmas Special, is The Caretaker.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:32.669
It’s self contained, so you can watch it
without knowing a lot about doctor who.

00:06:32.669 --> 00:06:36.110
And it’s very personal.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:37.930
Number 5 - Legend Of Korra

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:38.970
So sad to see this end.

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:42.870
If you never watched it, they just had the
series finale and set off this same sex relationship

00:06:42.870 --> 00:07:12.539
fire 
in 

00:07:12.539 --> 00:07:16.849
the fandom.

00:07:16.849 --> 00:07:20.229
Favorite Korra Episode This Year was Korra
Alone.

00:07:20.229 --> 00:07:25.400
It’s such a fun deep scan of where Korra
is at Psychologically, it features Katara

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:30.850
and it had the first appearance of Toph in
the new series.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:35.460
Number 4 - Sherlock

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:39.669
One of the best examples of the genius baby
that’s born when you combine some of the

00:07:39.669 --> 00:07:43.900
best actors in the world with the best set
design and the best writing.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:46.650
If you can’t tell I’m a huge fan of Martin
Freeman and Benedict Cumberbatch.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:49.889
There is a very good reason why they’re
the biggest actors on the planet right now.

00:07:49.889 --> 00:07:53.879
Which is also why it’s so hard for them
to make new sherlock episodes.

00:07:53.879 --> 00:07:58.139
Another huge thing to love about the series.

00:07:58.139 --> 00:07:59.199
Scarcity.

00:07:59.199 --> 00:08:06.780
Because they only do three 90 minute episodes,
there is no filler.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:11.169
American Television, by contrast, has 20+
weeks of episodes to fill.

00:08:11.169 --> 00:08:14.020
So the chances that everything will be amazing
is zero.

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:16.620
When you have 23 episodes a season, not everything
will be awesome.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:17.620
Sherlock on the other hand doesn’t have
that problem.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:20.639
My favorite episode this year was Episode
1 Empty Hearse.

00:08:20.639 --> 00:08:29.949
It’s just the right balance of drama 
and comedy.

00:08:29.949 --> 00:08:34.970
If you wanted to get your friend into sherlock,
first show them the sherlock tag on tumblr.

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:48.970
Not the johnlock tag, that’s only for advanced
fans who can handle some of the cringeworthy

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:49.970
fan fiction.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:52.920
Then show them Series 1 episode 1, Study in
Pink.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:58.080
I will do a few bonus Sherlock videos in January,
they’ll be filming the 2015 christmas special.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:03.920
So I’ll include new info as we get pictures
from the set.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.600
Number 3 - The Flash

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:10.130
Of all the new Comic Book Shows, this has
been my favorite.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:14.260
The characters are the best and the production
crew has created the most emotionally compelling

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.140
and interesting universes.

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:18.250
Technically it’s a shared universe with
arrow.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:21.240
But Flash is very different visually and tonally.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:24.660
There are a few of the bigger characters I
think still need some work like Iris and Eddie

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:28.410
but I think the back half of the season is
going to spend more time on them.

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:32.990
Harrison Wells is far and away my favorite
Comic Book TV Villain of the year.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:39.880
He’s a better villain right now than Ra’s
Al Gul, who in the comics is one of the best

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:42.120
Batman villains of all time.

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:51.380
That’s mostly because Wells is inside the
huddle, he’s in every episode and his motivations

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.380
are very complex.

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:56.130
He seems very evil but wants to protect the
hero at all costs.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:59.290
I don’t know if I can pick a single favorite
episode so far.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:05.190
But Episode 4, The Crossover, which is Episode
8 and Episode 9 are the best.

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:08.800
If you wanted to get your friend into this,
just start them with Episode 1.

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:15.090
Or, if they’re a comic book person, show
them the crossover episode.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:16.670
Number 2 - Arrow

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:18.660
Because arrow and flash exist in this shared
continuum.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:20.960
They share creative teams, they share a budget.

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:24.440
So both shows are equal in terms of quality.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:27.900
Arrow has just had more time to develop it’s
core characters and build out the internal

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:28.900
universe.

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:32.820
So I connect with it emotionally more than
the Flash.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:35.610
Stephen Amell is an amazing lead both on and
off the camera.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:43.560
My own experience with the show is a little
meta in that the actors and the network, the

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:46.280
CW network engage with me personally.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:50.780
Stephen Amell was the first big star to actually
reach out to me on social media to tell me

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:52.650
he liked my youtube channel.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:54.620
And I’m just a fan of the show.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:57.520
I’m not some huge media person.

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:01.510
Most actors don’t take the time to engage
with their fans, but because “The Captain”

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:07.590
as we call him, is so connected to the fandom
the other cast members have started to do

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:08.590
so too.

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:11.040
And that’s why shows like Supernatural have
endured for so long.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:16.770
Jared and Jensen actually interact with and
care about the people watching their show.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:21.390
My favorite Arrow Episode this year was Episode
9, the mid season finale.

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:22.390
It did the unthinkable.

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:29.360
It had the balls to kill off it’s main character.

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:35.000
Stephen Amell is a big Game of Thrones fan,
so you can think of this as your Arrow Ned

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.050
Stark moment.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:43.880
Number 1 - Game of Thrones

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:48.580
This goes without mentioning but the quality
of the production and the constant one-upsmanship

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:53.480
of each episode make this the best genre show
on tv right now.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:57.200
When I say genre I just mean, sci fi, fantasy,
horror, you get the idea.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:00.531
Remember how I said I really like Doctor Who
because it’s so different from other science

00:12:00.531 --> 00:12:01.531
fiction.

00:12:01.531 --> 00:12:04.090
It’s the same thing with Game of Thrones
and fantasy shows.

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:06.190
George RR Martin is really the person to thank
for that.

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:07.248
He would never have let them adapt it if they
didn’t stick pretty close to his original

00:12:07.248 --> 00:12:08.248
narrative.

00:12:08.248 --> 00:12:10.580
And yes, they are changing things in the future
but they’re only changing things to make

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.400
it linear and make it fit in 10 episodes a
year.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:18.180
It’s the same situation with South Park,
10 episodes means absolutely no filler.

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:21.850
Not every episode is Oberyn Martell vs The
Mountain, but there aren’t any clip shows.

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:23.710
My favorite episode was number 8.

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:26.460
I’ve rewatched the episodes a couple times
so I can’t remember what my favorite was

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:27.460
earlier this year.

00:12:27.460 --> 00:12:30.980
But Episode 8 Viper vs Mountain was one of
the most fun hours of television this year,

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:31.980
period.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:37.330
If you wanted to get someone into game of
thrones just have them start with season 1

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:38.330
episode 1.

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:42.800
It’s super serialized so starting in Season
5 will just confuse people.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.580
Season 5 is premiering April 5th.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:48.240
I’ve got a bunch of awesome videos planned
for each of the episodes and some really cool

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:49.240
giveaways.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:59.320
Seriously, Season 5 will melt your face off.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:51.279
Honorable Mention - Orphan Black, Constantine,

